"The stack points at line 22 of \u0060Orders.cs\u0060, which is the \u0060File.ReadLines(csvPath)\u0060 call in the constructor, so the crash happens before any order is parsed. Next I\u0027ll check how the path is built, whether the data file is tracked, and whether the repo has a deploy definition.The cause is hosting, not this method\u0027s code. I\u0027ve recorded it with high confidence.\n\n- **Where:** the \u0060OrderRepository\u0060 constructor, \u0060src/OrderService/Orders.cs\u0060 line 22 (\u0060File.ReadLines(csvPath)\u0060), called from \u0060Program.cs\u0060 line 8.\n- **Why it isn\u0027t the get-order code:** the exception is thrown while the repository is being built, before \u0060GetOrder\u0060 runs. \u0060Api/GetOrder.cs\u0060 and the parser never execute for this request.\n- **Path:** \u0060Program.cs\u0060 passes the relative path \u0060Path.Combine(\u0022data\u0022, \u0022orders.csv\u0022)\u0060, which resolves against the process working directory. The error shows that directory was \u0060/app\u0060, so the process looked for \u0060/app/data/orders.csv\u0060 and didn\u0027t find it.\n- **Data file:** \u0060data/orders.csv\u0060 (960 B) is in the repo at the sample root and is tracked in git. So the file exists in the source; it is not present at the path the deployed process uses. Nothing in the repo (no Dockerfile or deploy script was found) shows how the deploy places the file.\n- **Not a known regression:** the only commit touching \u0060Program.cs\u0060 and \u0060orders.csv\u0060 is \u0060916d807f5\u0060 (2026-11-08, the sample\u0027s initial commit), so nothing recent changed the path.\n\nThis points at the runbook\u0027s hand-off rule (missing data file or where it is deployed \u2192 ops). It should go to ops to confirm the working directory of the deployed process and that \u0060data/orders.csv\u0060 sits beside the service there. The code\u0027s \u0060Items[0]\u0060 access in \u0060GetOrder.cs\u0060 would throw for an order with no items, but that is not what happened in this run, so I left it out of the cause.\n\n[Answered by triage.investigator, did: FindFiles: Found 222 file(s) matching \u0027*\u0027:; ReadWorkspaceFile: using System.Globalization;; ReadWorkspaceFile: using System.Globalization;; SearchWorkspace: demos/louis-agent/samples/order-service/tests/OrderService.Tests/OrderApiTests.\u2026; FindFiles: No files matching pattern \u0027*ockerfile*\u0027 found.; ReadWorkspaceFile: bin/; ReadWorkspaceFile: namespace OrderService;; ReadWorkspaceFile: namespace OrderService;; FileHistory: 916d807f5  2026-11-08  Louis Marais  feat(f106.3.1): step 1 - the order-service\u2026; FileHistory: 916d807f5  2026-11-08  Louis Marais  feat(f106.3.1): step 1 - the order-service\u2026; ReportInvestigation: Recorded step 2 of run eval-get-order-1001-20261127-060003-triage-1: The invest\u2026]"